WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.623
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off.

00:00:16.624 --> 00:00:18.696
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:20.008
The family business.

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:24.061
You still running credit-card scams?

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:25.453
You think credit-card fraud is easy?

00:00:25.454 --> 00:00:27.553
- Okay, Mr. Burkowitz.
- Federal marshals.

00:00:27.554 --> 00:00:29.460
- Environmental study majors.
- I'm father Simmons.

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:31.355
U.S. Wildlife service.
Nigel Tuffnel.

00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:34.161
- Dr. Jerry Kaplan. Art dealers. Rangers.
- Reporters. Students.

00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:37.280
- Fraternity brothers.
- Homeland security? Pretty illegal, even for us.

00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:40.066
<i>S.W.A.T. team discovered
a local woman bound and gagged.</i>

00:00:40.069 --> 00:00:44.027
<i>Her attacker, a white male
approximately 24 to 30 years of age,</i>

00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:46.606
- <i>was discovered hiding in the home.</i>
- Shapeshifter?

00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:48.683
Every culture in the world
has a shapeshifter lore,

00:00:48.686 --> 00:00:52.091
legends of creatures who can transform
themselves into animals or other men.

00:00:57.416 --> 00:01:01.493
Cops are blaming this Dean Winchester guy
for Emily's murder.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.312
- Sorry I'm gonna miss it.
- Miss what?

00:01:03.377 --> 00:01:05.682
How many chances am I gonna have
to see my own funeral?

00:01:17.975 --> 00:01:18.973
Under what name?

00:01:19.697 --> 00:01:22.333
Oh, yeah, that's my favorite so far.

00:01:23.245 --> 00:01:25.731
Possible I.D.S in three states
that we know of.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:30.670
I got to call you back.

00:01:38.048 --> 00:01:38.870
Wow.

00:01:41.837 --> 00:01:44.242
First I thought
you were just stepping up your game.

00:01:45.215 --> 00:01:46.421
Credit-card fraud,

00:01:47.026 --> 00:01:49.242
breaking and entering.
This one,

00:01:49.468 --> 00:01:50.550
a puzzle...

00:01:50.957 --> 00:01:52.443
Grave desecration.

00:01:54.076 --> 00:01:57.092
But still, these are a long way from murder.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.282
Then we get a fax from St. Louis...

00:02:02.065 --> 00:02:05.550
where you're suspected of torturing
and murdering a young woman.

00:02:06.587 --> 00:02:09.291
However, no one could prove anything,
of course, because

00:02:09.298 --> 00:02:11.053
supposedly you died there.

00:02:14.415 --> 00:02:15.981
But I got to tell you something.

00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:19.803
You look pretty healthy to me.

00:02:23.397 --> 00:02:27.063
So, now we know Karen Giles
wasn't the first person you murdered.

00:02:27.516 --> 00:02:29.632
Going somewhere, Sam?

00:02:31.278 --> 00:02:33.370
But I guarantee you she's the last.

00:02:42.796 --> 00:02:44.300
Transcript : Raceman

00:02:44.358 --> 00:02:45.853
Titelilie
www.forom.com

00:02:56.168 --> 00:02:57.613
Thought you might be thirsty.

00:02:57.615 --> 00:02:59.222
Okay, so you're the good cop.

00:03:00.518 --> 00:03:03.073
- Where's the bad cop?
- He's with your brother.

00:03:03.076 --> 00:03:05.180
Okay. And you're holding us why?

00:03:05.188 --> 00:03:07.313
He's being held on suspicion of murder.

00:03:07.318 --> 00:03:10.083
- And you? We'll see.
- Murder?

00:03:10.086 --> 00:03:12.653
You sound genuinely surprised.

00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:14.793
Or are you that good of an actor?

00:03:14.807 --> 00:03:16.350
Who is he supposed to have murdered?

00:03:16.356 --> 00:03:18.562
- We'll get around to that.
- You can't just hold us here

00:03:18.578 --> 00:03:21.852
- without formal charges.
- Actually, we can for 48 hours.

00:03:21.855 --> 00:03:24.412
But you, being a prelaw student,
would know that.

00:03:25.896 --> 00:03:27.453
I know all about you, Sam.

00:03:28.747 --> 00:03:30.143
You're 23 years old.

00:03:30.345 --> 00:03:32.131
No job, no home address.

00:03:33.155 --> 00:03:35.052
Your mother died when you were a baby.

00:03:35.588 --> 00:03:38.022
Your father's whereabouts are unknown.

00:03:38.197 --> 00:03:39.543
And then there's

00:03:39.548 --> 00:03:41.153
the case of your brother, Dean,

00:03:41.936 --> 00:03:44.731
whose demise was, well,
just a little bit exaggerated.

00:03:44.738 --> 00:03:46.801
Feel free to jump in whenever you like.

00:03:49.075 --> 00:03:50.132
Shy?

00:03:50.137 --> 00:03:51.263
No problem.

00:03:51.265 --> 00:03:52.292
I'll keep going.

00:03:52.725 --> 00:03:55.143
Your family moved around a lot
when you were a kid.

00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:57.951
Despite that, you were a straight-A student.

00:03:58.066 --> 00:04:00.561
Got into Stanford with a full ride.

00:04:03.646 --> 00:04:05.163
Then about a year ago,

00:04:05.166 --> 00:04:06.870
there was a fire in your apartment.

00:04:06.876 --> 00:04:08.243
One fatality...

00:04:08.245 --> 00:04:09.461
Jessica Moore,

00:04:09.607 --> 00:04:10.713
your girlfriend.

00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:15.673
After she died, you fell off the grid,
left behind everything.

00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:17.492
I needed some time off...

00:04:18.638 --> 00:04:20.051
to deal.

00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:23.942
So I'm taking a road trip with my brother.

00:04:23.946 --> 00:04:26.382
- How's that going for you?
- Great.

00:04:27.558 --> 00:04:28.701
I mean...

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:33.192
we saw the second-largest ball of twine
in the continental US.

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:35.312
Awesome.

00:04:37.178 --> 00:04:39.861
We ran Dean's fingerprints through iafis.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:43.201
Got over a dozen possible hits.

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:45.903
"Possible" hits, which makes them worthless.

00:04:45.905 --> 00:04:47.293
But makes you wonder,

00:04:47.566 --> 00:04:50.043
what are we gonna find
when we run your prints?

00:04:50.288 --> 00:04:51.933
Yeah, well, uh...

00:04:52.528 --> 00:04:54.440
you be sure to let me know, all right?

00:04:55.038 --> 00:04:56.061
May I?

00:04:56.125 --> 00:04:57.721
- Please.
- Great.

00:05:04.075 --> 00:05:06.161
Sam, you seem like a good kid.

00:05:06.428 --> 00:05:08.431
It's not your fault Dean's your brother.

00:05:08.438 --> 00:05:10.303
We can't pick our family.

00:05:11.408 --> 00:05:14.430
Right now detectives in St. Louis
are exhuming a corpse.

00:05:14.436 --> 00:05:17.521
They're trying to figure out
how your brother faked his own death

00:05:17.686 --> 00:05:20.160
after torturing all those young women.

00:05:20.357 --> 00:05:22.133
Dean's a bad guy.

00:05:22.148 --> 00:05:23.713
His life is over.

00:05:24.276 --> 00:05:26.122
Yours doesn't have to be.

00:05:28.285 --> 00:05:30.721
You want me to turn against my own brother?

00:05:30.735 --> 00:05:33.713
No.
We already caught him cold,

00:05:34.087 --> 00:05:37.042
red-handed at the Karen Giles murder scene.

00:05:38.557 --> 00:05:40.620
We just need you

00:05:40.785 --> 00:05:42.671
to fill in some missing pieces.

00:05:43.598 --> 00:05:45.201
Why would I do that?

00:05:48.565 --> 00:05:50.920
Because I can talk to the D.A.,

00:05:50.928 --> 00:05:52.513
make a deal for you.

00:05:52.896 --> 00:05:54.652
You can get on with your life.

00:05:55.357 --> 00:05:57.051
Dean's as good as gone.

00:06:03.717 --> 00:06:06.663
My dad and Tony Giles were old friends.

00:06:07.428 --> 00:06:09.830
They were in the service together.

00:06:09.837 --> 00:06:12.550
We've known him since we were kids,
you know?

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.330
So we came as soon as we heard
about his death.

00:06:21.215 --> 00:06:22.771
Here you go.

00:06:23.365 --> 00:06:25.911
- Anthony Giles.
- Who's Anthony Giles?

00:06:26.175 --> 00:06:28.042
The Baltimore lawyer.

00:06:28.108 --> 00:06:29.821
Working late at office. Check it out.

00:06:33.248 --> 00:06:35.550
"His throat was slit but the room was clean"

00:06:36.526 --> 00:06:39.381
- Huh. No dna, no prints.
- Keep reading. It gets better.

00:06:39.607 --> 00:06:42.912
"Security cameras failed to capture footage
of the assailant"

00:06:43.778 --> 00:06:45.461
Either somebody tampered with the tapes...

00:06:45.465 --> 00:06:46.941
or it's an invisible killer.

00:06:47.478 --> 00:06:48.573
My favorite kind.

00:06:48.996 --> 00:06:50.462
What do you think, Scully?
We check it out?

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.191
I'm not Scully. You're Scully.

00:06:52.735 --> 00:06:53.673
No, I'm Mulder.

00:06:54.106 --> 00:06:55.340
You're a redheaded woman.

00:06:56.308 --> 00:06:57.082
So...

00:06:58.318 --> 00:07:00.432
It would've been hard for Dean
to kill Tony,

00:07:00.435 --> 00:07:02.571
considering we weren't in town
at the time.

00:07:02.575 --> 00:07:04.101
So, tell me what happened next.

00:07:04.305 --> 00:07:05.652
Okay, uh,

00:07:05.997 --> 00:07:07.660
that's when we went to see Karen.

00:07:07.976 --> 00:07:09.743
She was barely holding it together.

00:07:10.237 --> 00:07:12.383
We just wanted to be there for her,
you know?

00:07:14.615 --> 00:07:16.343
Insurance.

00:07:17.548 --> 00:07:19.581
I totally forgot about the insurance.

00:07:20.775 --> 00:07:22.641
We're very sorry to bother you
right now, but

00:07:23.665 --> 00:07:26.662
the company is required
to conduct its own investigation.

00:07:26.668 --> 00:07:28.430
- You understand?
- Sure.

00:07:29.627 --> 00:07:31.290
If you could just tell us anything

00:07:31.296 --> 00:07:33.333
you remember about the night
your husband died.

00:07:34.305 --> 00:07:36.140
Tony and I were supposed to have dinner.

00:07:36.147 --> 00:07:39.170
He called and said that he was having
computer troubles

00:07:39.521 --> 00:07:41.266
and that he had to work late.

00:07:42.739 --> 00:07:44.247
That was it.

00:07:45.352 --> 00:07:48.116
Do you have any idea
who could've done this to him?

00:07:48.709 --> 00:07:52.062
No. It's like i told the police. I...

00:07:52.368 --> 00:07:53.852
I have no idea.

00:07:53.868 --> 00:07:55.500
Did Tony mention anything

00:07:55.505 --> 00:07:56.881
unusual

00:07:57.127 --> 00:07:59.390
to you in the days before his death?

00:08:00.207 --> 00:08:01.531
Unusual?

00:08:01.958 --> 00:08:03.971
Yeah, like strange.

00:08:06.086 --> 00:08:08.220
- Strange?
- You know, Karen, weird.

00:08:08.377 --> 00:08:10.101
Weird noises,

00:08:10.445 --> 00:08:12.541
visions, anything like that?

00:08:19.295 --> 00:08:22.282
He had a nightmare the day before he died.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:25.001
What kind of a nightmare?

00:08:25.968 --> 00:08:28.071
Uh, he said that he woke up
in the middle of the night,

00:08:28.075 --> 00:08:30.530
and there was a woman standing at
the foot of the bed.

00:08:31.288 --> 00:08:34.621
He blinked. She was gone.
I mean, it was just a nightmare.

00:08:35.557 --> 00:08:37.071
Did he say what she looked like?

00:08:39.006 --> 00:08:41.722
What the helle difference does it make
what she looked like?!

00:08:45.528 --> 00:08:47.903
Uh, it's just our company is very thorough.

00:08:49.446 --> 00:08:52.133
He said she was pale,
and she had dark, red eyes.

00:08:53.476 --> 00:08:54.981
So I gave Karen a hug,

00:08:55.867 --> 00:08:57.961
told her to call me
if she needed anything, and

00:08:58.728 --> 00:08:59.590
that was it.

00:09:00.435 --> 00:09:01.593
End of story.

00:09:03.397 --> 00:09:05.841
Sam, I am trying to help you here,

00:09:06.088 --> 00:09:08.631
but you have got to be honest with me.

00:09:09.605 --> 00:09:11.610
Now, we have an eyewitness,

00:09:11.825 --> 00:09:13.920
someone who saw two men

00:09:14.325 --> 00:09:17.750
fitting your and your brother's description
breaking into Giles' office.

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:18.800
Ok, look,

00:09:19.026 --> 00:09:22.403
Karen called us later, said that there was
some stuff she wanted from Tony's office,

00:09:22.406 --> 00:09:24.072
but the police weren't letting her in.

00:09:24.578 --> 00:09:27.872
Like a picture of the two of them in Paris
and some other stuff.

00:09:28.177 --> 00:09:30.463
Look, it was wrong to enter a crime scene,
but

00:09:30.466 --> 00:09:31.900
she gave us the key.

00:09:44.837 --> 00:09:45.772
Hey.

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:49.032
Anthony Giles' body was found
right about here.

00:09:49.745 --> 00:09:51.411
"Throat slit so deep,"

00:09:51.418 --> 00:09:53.153
"that part of his spinal cord was visible".

00:09:54.736 --> 00:09:56.050
What do you think?

00:09:56.058 --> 00:09:57.471
Vengeful spirit?

00:09:57.478 --> 00:09:59.760
- Underline "vengeful"?
- Yeah. Maybe.

00:10:00.428 --> 00:10:03.041
I mean, he did see that woman
at the foot of his bed.

00:10:07.346 --> 00:10:08.692
Look at this.

00:10:11.787 --> 00:10:13.061
"danashulps"

00:10:13.885 --> 00:10:15.540
What's that, a name?

00:10:17.188 --> 00:10:18.832
I don't know, but it's everywhere.

00:10:21.818 --> 00:10:25.180
"All work and no play makes Jack
a dull boy"

00:10:45.676 --> 00:10:48.591
I'd say we've officially crossed over
into weird.

00:10:48.837 --> 00:10:50.153
Maybe Giles knew her.

00:10:50.158 --> 00:10:52.953
Maybe it's the name of our pale,
red-eyed mystery girl.

00:10:53.175 --> 00:10:54.272
Well...

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:56.721
let's see what we can see.

00:11:02.787 --> 00:11:05.082
There's not a single mention of
a Dana Shulps anywhere.

00:11:05.556 --> 00:11:06.821
There's not a D. Shulps

00:11:06.825 --> 00:11:08.362
or any other kind of freaking Shulps.

00:11:08.368 --> 00:11:09.351
Great.

00:11:09.358 --> 00:11:10.922
- What do you got?
- Nothing.

00:11:10.925 --> 00:11:15.690
No Dana Shulps has ever lived or died
in Baltimore in the last 50 years at least.

00:11:15.698 --> 00:11:17.543
- So, what now?
- Well,

00:11:17.547 --> 00:11:19.643
I think I'm pretty close
to cracking Giles' password.

00:11:19.647 --> 00:11:21.511
Maybe there's something
in his personal files, you know.

00:11:21.515 --> 00:11:22.822
By "close" you mean...

00:11:23.177 --> 00:11:24.361
30 minutes maybe.

00:11:27.025 --> 00:11:28.112
Awesome.

00:11:29.697 --> 00:11:31.520
So, I guess I just get to, uh,

00:11:32.056 --> 00:11:33.270
hang out.

00:11:33.397 --> 00:11:34.390
That's

00:11:34.445 --> 00:11:35.460
awesome.

00:11:49.447 --> 00:11:50.602
Dude, seriously.

00:11:50.608 --> 00:11:52.182
Alright. I'm gonna go talk to Karen again,

00:11:52.186 --> 00:11:54.320
see if she knows anything about
this Dana Shulps, huh?

00:11:54.606 --> 00:11:55.373
Great.

00:11:56.608 --> 00:11:57.751
Keep going, sparky.

00:11:59.317 --> 00:12:01.990
Then Dean went back to Karen's place
to check up on her.

00:12:02.128 --> 00:12:03.110
I mean,

00:12:03.366 --> 00:12:05.381
you know,
she had been pretty upset earlier.

00:12:05.397 --> 00:12:07.000
So why didn't you go with him?

00:12:08.277 --> 00:12:10.251
I just went back to the motel.

00:12:11.435 --> 00:12:13.403
How did you know I was there,
by the way?

00:12:13.845 --> 00:12:17.352
We found the motel matchbook on your brother
when we arrested him.

00:12:19.586 --> 00:12:21.330
Let's quit fooling around.

00:12:21.765 --> 00:12:24.570
Now, you were with your brother
the whole time you were in Baltimore.

00:12:24.575 --> 00:12:26.583
Why separate now?

00:12:26.836 --> 00:12:29.303
Because your brother left you
to go murder Karen.

00:12:29.307 --> 00:12:33.223
- He didn't kill anyone.
- I heard the 911 call!

00:12:33.227 --> 00:12:36.942
Karen was terrified!
She said someone was in the house.

00:13:46.205 --> 00:13:48.702
<i>- Emergency services.</i>
- Hello?

00:13:48.705 --> 00:13:50.690
I think I saw somebody in my house.

00:13:50.698 --> 00:13:52.031
<i>What is your address, ma'am?

00:13:52.036 --> 00:13:54.031
It's 421 Clinton avenue.

00:13:54.966 --> 00:13:56.120
Please...

00:13:56.868 --> 00:13:57.730
Hello?

00:14:50.946 --> 00:14:52.152
Karen, are you in there?

00:15:45.158 --> 00:15:46.263
Oh, god.

00:15:59.466 --> 00:16:00.980
Seriously, what the hell?

00:16:19.845 --> 00:16:21.090
Freeze.

00:16:21.277 --> 00:16:22.393
Stay on your knees.

00:16:22.926 --> 00:16:24.321
Hands where I can see them.

00:16:24.696 --> 00:16:25.720
Now!

00:16:27.518 --> 00:16:28.670
Cuff him.

00:16:41.578 --> 00:16:43.022
You getting anywhere with him?

00:16:43.297 --> 00:16:44.183
No.

00:16:44.707 --> 00:16:46.693
Just a lot of wise ass remarks.

00:16:46.697 --> 00:16:47.703
You?

00:16:48.417 --> 00:16:51.213
Sam's story matches Dean's
to the last detail.

00:16:52.388 --> 00:16:54.603
Yeah, well, these guys are good.

00:16:54.976 --> 00:16:56.151
I'll give them that.

00:16:58.186 --> 00:17:02.221
If we don't get Sam to flip, we have nothing
but a lot of circumstantial evidence.

00:17:02.235 --> 00:17:05.520
We got Dean at the crime scene
with blood on his hands.

00:17:05.885 --> 00:17:07.912
Juries have convicted for less.

00:17:08.495 --> 00:17:11.383
Yeah, but, I mean,
where is the murder weapon?

00:17:11.798 --> 00:17:14.353
What's the motive?
You talk about reasonable doubt.

00:17:14.357 --> 00:17:15.122
Diana...

00:17:16.405 --> 00:17:17.340
do you

00:17:17.418 --> 00:17:18.572
have reasonable doubt?

00:17:23.996 --> 00:17:26.943
We keep leaning on these guys,
one of them will tumble.

00:17:26.948 --> 00:17:28.913
And don't forget about St. Louis.

00:17:29.987 --> 00:17:30.852
I'm telling you,

00:17:30.935 --> 00:17:32.142
this Dean guy

00:17:32.146 --> 00:17:33.163
is our guy.

00:17:34.335 --> 00:17:36.520
I know Tony Giles was a friend of yours.

00:17:36.525 --> 00:17:38.450
Yeah, he was. He was a good friend.

00:17:38.458 --> 00:17:41.143
I know you want to clean this mess up quick,

00:17:41.626 --> 00:17:44.371
but come on.
Tony knew a lot of criminal types.

00:17:44.377 --> 00:17:46.912
- Maybe we just...
- "Criminal types"?

00:17:47.566 --> 00:17:51.522
He was a defense lawyer, for god sakes.
Of course he knew criminal types.

00:17:52.516 --> 00:17:53.530
Okay.

00:17:53.916 --> 00:17:56.490
- All right. Let's get back at them.
- No. You know what?

00:17:56.687 --> 00:17:58.842
Let them stew in their juices for a bit.

00:18:05.158 --> 00:18:06.410
Come here.

00:18:21.868 --> 00:18:24.993
Dana Shulps, Dana Shulps,
Dana Shulps...

00:18:35.237 --> 00:18:36.891
Maybe it's not a name.

00:18:37.686 --> 00:18:39.521
Maybe it's not a name?

00:18:40.337 --> 00:18:41.842
Anagram maybe?

00:18:58.445 --> 00:18:59.470
Mr. Winchester?

00:18:59.627 --> 00:19:00.450
Yeah.

00:19:00.657 --> 00:19:02.010
I'm Jeff Crouse.

00:19:02.956 --> 00:19:05.102
I'm with the public defender's office.

00:19:06.305 --> 00:19:07.553
I'm your lawyer.

00:19:08.005 --> 00:19:10.542
Oh, thank god. I'm saved.

00:19:12.097 --> 00:19:14.540
Can I, uh, steal a pen from you
and some paper?

00:19:14.548 --> 00:19:15.342
Sure.

00:19:17.318 --> 00:19:18.323
Well,

00:19:18.327 --> 00:19:19.142
the

00:19:19.146 --> 00:19:20.990
police haven't found a weapon yet.

00:19:21.527 --> 00:19:22.693
So that's good.

00:19:23.438 --> 00:19:24.420
But, uh,

00:19:24.425 --> 00:19:25.901
they got your prints

00:19:26.295 --> 00:19:27.781
and literally

00:19:28.616 --> 00:19:30.351
blood on your hands. And

00:19:31.226 --> 00:19:32.393
with your police record...

00:19:35.598 --> 00:19:36.972
Mr. Winchester,

00:19:37.398 --> 00:19:39.950
- what are you doing?
- I think it's an anagram.

00:19:40.256 --> 00:19:43.622
- A what?
- An anagram. Same letters, different words.

00:19:45.308 --> 00:19:46.561
Could you do me a favor?

00:19:47.287 --> 00:19:49.532
See if you recognize any
of these words, you know.

00:19:49.537 --> 00:19:51.962
Local names, places, anything like that.

00:19:53.177 --> 00:19:55.742
Do you understand how serious
these charges are?

00:19:57.315 --> 00:19:59.533
I'm handcuffed to a table. Yeah. I get it.

00:19:59.616 --> 00:20:01.822
Humor me. Take a quick look.

00:20:09.216 --> 00:20:11.652
Well, S-U-P?
I don't know about that, but...

00:20:12.986 --> 00:20:14.321
Ashland is

00:20:14.327 --> 00:20:15.813
is a street name.

00:20:16.086 --> 00:20:17.583
It's not far from here.

00:20:17.588 --> 00:20:18.461
Street?

00:20:20.458 --> 00:20:24.362
Let's start with where you were
the night that Anthony Giles died.

00:20:24.368 --> 00:20:25.932
Can you get in to see my brother?

00:20:25.938 --> 00:20:27.410
Mr. Winchester...

00:20:28.258 --> 00:20:30.722
you could be facing
the death penalty here.

00:20:30.928 --> 00:20:33.073
Hey, thanks for the law review, Matlock.

00:20:33.628 --> 00:20:35.663
But if you want to help me...

00:20:38.535 --> 00:20:40.340
I need you to see my brother.

00:21:24.138 --> 00:21:25.513
I hope that was meaningful.

00:21:26.715 --> 00:21:28.851
But I'd like to discuss your case now.

00:21:29.565 --> 00:21:31.071
Sure thing, Matlock.

00:21:32.147 --> 00:21:34.322
You two really are brothers, aren't you?

00:21:35.078 --> 00:21:36.041
Now...

00:21:36.897 --> 00:21:38.023
as you know,

00:21:38.688 --> 00:21:40.931
the D.A. might be interested in...

00:21:43.358 --> 00:21:45.430
We need you with the other one.

00:21:53.316 --> 00:21:54.951
This should be nice.

00:21:59.038 --> 00:22:00.112
Counselor...

00:22:01.288 --> 00:22:02.961
your boy decided to confess.

00:22:03.087 --> 00:22:04.422
Mr. Winchester,

00:22:05.107 --> 00:22:07.042
I would advise against that strongly.

00:22:07.075 --> 00:22:08.850
Talk directly into the camera.

00:22:08.858 --> 00:22:10.743
Start by stating your name for the record.

00:22:14.658 --> 00:22:16.430
My name is Dean Winchester.

00:22:17.196 --> 00:22:18.491
I'm an aquarius.

00:22:18.496 --> 00:22:21.201
I enjoy sunsets, long walks on the beach,

00:22:21.207 --> 00:22:22.570
and frisky women.

00:22:23.368 --> 00:22:24.990
And I did not kill anyone,

00:22:25.637 --> 00:22:26.980
but I know who did.

00:22:26.987 --> 00:22:28.553
Or rather what did.

00:22:29.167 --> 00:22:30.613
Of course, it can't be for sure

00:22:30.618 --> 00:22:32.572
because our investigation was interrupted.

00:22:33.435 --> 00:22:34.730
But our working theory

00:22:34.825 --> 00:22:36.372
is that we're looking for some kind of

00:22:36.638 --> 00:22:38.202
vengeful spirit.

00:22:38.448 --> 00:22:39.712
Excuse me?

00:22:40.177 --> 00:22:42.041
You know, Casper, the bloodthirsty ghost.

00:22:43.856 --> 00:22:45.042
Tony Giles saw it.

00:22:45.358 --> 00:22:47.523
I'll bet you cash money Karen did, too.

00:22:47.618 --> 00:22:50.121
See, the interesting thing is the word
it leaves behind.

00:22:50.125 --> 00:22:51.090
For some reason,

00:22:51.096 --> 00:22:52.601
it's trying to tell us something.

00:22:53.688 --> 00:22:55.583
But communicating across a veil

00:22:56.305 --> 00:22:57.332
ain't easy.

00:22:57.948 --> 00:23:00.420
And sometimes the spirits,
they get things jumbled.

00:23:00.836 --> 00:23:02.010
You remember "Redrum".

00:23:02.568 --> 00:23:03.500
Same concept.

00:23:04.107 --> 00:23:04.961
You know,

00:23:05.488 --> 00:23:06.890
it could be word fragments.

00:23:07.116 --> 00:23:08.280
Other times...

00:23:11.796 --> 00:23:12.651
It's anagrams.

00:23:13.748 --> 00:23:15.980
See, at first we thought
this was a name, Dana Shulps.

00:23:17.306 --> 00:23:18.161
But now

00:23:18.506 --> 00:23:19.890
we think it's a street.

00:23:19.896 --> 00:23:20.901
Ashland.

00:23:21.097 --> 00:23:22.471
Whatever is going on,

00:23:23.556 --> 00:23:27.182
- I'm betting it started there.
- You arrogant bastard.

00:23:27.876 --> 00:23:30.730
Tony and Karen were good people,
and you're making jokes.

00:23:30.735 --> 00:23:32.352
I'm not joking, Ponch.

00:23:34.347 --> 00:23:38.400
You murdered them in cold blood
just like that girl in St. Louis.

00:23:38.408 --> 00:23:39.933
Oh, yeah, that wasn't me, either.

00:23:39.937 --> 00:23:42.563
That was a shapeshifter creature
that only looked like me.

00:23:46.208 --> 00:23:47.652
Pete, that is enough!

00:23:49.465 --> 00:23:50.542
You asked for the truth.

00:23:53.677 --> 00:23:54.822
Lock this guy off.

00:24:07.767 --> 00:24:08.950
What the hell?

00:24:10.757 --> 00:24:12.023
Where is he?

00:24:21.347 --> 00:24:22.162
How did he do it?

00:24:23.005 --> 00:24:24.491
The fire escape's way over...

00:24:26.675 --> 00:24:28.821
- What?
- These two guys.

00:24:32.798 --> 00:24:34.110
Hilts and Mcqueen?

00:24:34.506 --> 00:24:35.370
What is that?

00:24:35.428 --> 00:24:38.033
Hilts is Steve Mcqueen's character in
"The Great Escape".

00:25:36.266 --> 00:25:37.781
Can we make this quick?

00:25:37.898 --> 00:25:40.592
I'm really tired.
It's been a long day, you know,

00:25:40.595 --> 00:25:42.211
with your partner assaulting me and all.

00:25:42.506 --> 00:25:44.592
I want to know more about that stuff

00:25:44.596 --> 00:25:47.033
- you were talking about earlier.
- Time life,

00:25:47.216 --> 00:25:48.692
"mysteries of the unknown".

00:25:48.898 --> 00:25:50.113
Look it up.

00:25:54.857 --> 00:25:56.892
Let's pretend for the moment

00:25:57.415 --> 00:25:59.583
you're not entirely insane.

00:26:00.428 --> 00:26:04.272
What would one of these things
be doing here?

00:26:04.278 --> 00:26:05.933
Vengeful spirit?

00:26:08.707 --> 00:26:11.341
Well, they're created by violent deaths,

00:26:11.638 --> 00:26:14.493
and then they come back for a reason,
usually a nasty one,

00:26:14.498 --> 00:26:16.663
like revenge on the people that hurt them.

00:26:17.687 --> 00:26:19.583
And, uh, these

00:26:19.796 --> 00:26:21.253
spirits...

00:26:22.287 --> 00:26:24.571
They're capable of killing people.

00:26:29.818 --> 00:26:31.252
Where did you get that?

00:26:37.197 --> 00:26:38.121
I don't know.

00:26:39.905 --> 00:26:41.082
It wasn't there before.

00:26:42.955 --> 00:26:44.432
You've seen it, haven't you?

00:26:45.325 --> 00:26:46.212
The spirit.

00:26:46.325 --> 00:26:47.422
How did you know?

00:26:47.646 --> 00:26:50.090
Because Karen had the same bruises
on her wrists.

00:26:51.046 --> 00:26:54.061
I'm willing to bet that if you look at
Giles' autopsy photos, he's got them, too.

00:26:54.068 --> 00:26:55.683
It's got something to do with the spirit.

00:26:56.006 --> 00:26:57.403
I don't know what.

00:27:02.107 --> 00:27:02.883
I know.

00:27:04.096 --> 00:27:05.372
You think you're going crazy.

00:27:05.967 --> 00:27:07.611
But let's skip that part, shall we?

00:27:08.567 --> 00:27:10.833
Because the last two people
who saw this thing

00:27:11.256 --> 00:27:12.681
died pretty soon after.

00:27:14.797 --> 00:27:15.790
You hear me?

00:27:18.945 --> 00:27:20.611
You think I'm gonna die.

00:27:20.655 --> 00:27:21.952
You need to go to Sam.

00:27:23.146 --> 00:27:24.530
He'll help.

00:27:26.555 --> 00:27:28.092
You're giving your brother up.

00:27:28.545 --> 00:27:31.032
Go to the first motel listed
in the yellow pages.

00:27:31.207 --> 00:27:32.191
Look for Jim Rockford.

00:27:32.197 --> 00:27:33.973
That's how we find each other
when we're separated.

00:27:34.338 --> 00:27:35.772
You can arrest him, if you want.

00:27:36.587 --> 00:27:37.940
Or you can let him save your life.

00:27:55.896 --> 00:27:57.431
These showed up after you saw it?

00:27:57.596 --> 00:27:58.461
Yeah,

00:27:58.728 --> 00:28:00.362
- I guess.
- All right.

00:28:01.356 --> 00:28:03.503
You're gonna have to tell me
exactly what you saw.

00:28:04.657 --> 00:28:06.611
You know, I must be losing my mind.

00:28:08.176 --> 00:28:09.573
You're a fugitive.

00:28:09.625 --> 00:28:11.061
I should be arresting you.

00:28:11.065 --> 00:28:12.352
All right, well,

00:28:12.616 --> 00:28:14.632
you know what?
You can arrest me later, alright?

00:28:14.637 --> 00:28:15.991
After you live through this.

00:28:16.175 --> 00:28:18.111
But right now, you got to talk to me.

00:28:18.306 --> 00:28:19.463
Okay?

00:28:21.998 --> 00:28:23.011
Okay. Great.

00:28:23.285 --> 00:28:25.230
Now, the spirit, what did it look like?

00:28:25.235 --> 00:28:26.492
She was, um,

00:28:27.407 --> 00:28:28.661
really pale...

00:28:29.488 --> 00:28:31.140
and her throat was cut.

00:28:31.215 --> 00:28:34.023
And her eyes, they were like this deep,
dark red.

00:28:34.025 --> 00:28:36.633
It appeared like
she was trying to talk to me,

00:28:36.795 --> 00:28:38.273
but she couldn't.

00:28:39.077 --> 00:28:40.481
It was just...

00:28:40.485 --> 00:28:42.180
a lot of blood.

00:28:44.475 --> 00:28:45.952
You know what? Here.

00:28:45.956 --> 00:28:49.390
I've been researching every girl who has ever
died or gone missing from Ashland street.

00:28:51.695 --> 00:28:53.121
How did you get those?

00:28:53.128 --> 00:28:55.641
Those are from crime scenes
and booking photos.

00:28:56.636 --> 00:28:58.851
You have your job. I have mine.

00:28:59.786 --> 00:29:03.100
Here. I need you to look through these.
Tell me if you recognize anyone.

00:29:16.156 --> 00:29:17.233
This is her.

00:29:17.398 --> 00:29:18.471
I'm sure of it.

00:29:19.925 --> 00:29:21.111
Claire Becker?

00:29:21.787 --> 00:29:25.010
28 years old, disappeared about
eight or nine months ago.

00:29:25.017 --> 00:29:26.501
But I don't even know her.

00:29:26.505 --> 00:29:28.411
Why would she come after me?

00:29:28.416 --> 00:29:29.280
Well,

00:29:29.567 --> 00:29:32.213
before her death,
she was arrested twice

00:29:32.217 --> 00:29:33.410
for dealing heroin.

00:29:33.768 --> 00:29:35.482
- You ever work narcotics?
- Yeah,

00:29:35.488 --> 00:29:36.452
Pete and I did,

00:29:36.605 --> 00:29:37.912
before homicide.

00:29:38.585 --> 00:29:39.881
You ever bust her?

00:29:39.945 --> 00:29:41.320
Not that I remember.

00:29:44.825 --> 00:29:47.733
Says she was last seen entering
2911 Ashland street.

00:29:47.735 --> 00:29:49.270
Police searched the place,

00:29:49.798 --> 00:29:51.062
didn't find anything.

00:29:53.608 --> 00:29:55.050
Guess we got to check it out ourselves,

00:29:55.427 --> 00:29:56.720
see if we can find her body.

00:29:58.046 --> 00:29:58.803
What?

00:30:01.317 --> 00:30:03.103
Well, we got to salt and burn her bones.

00:30:03.536 --> 00:30:05.030
It's the only way to put her spirit to rest.

00:30:05.715 --> 00:30:06.932
Of course it is.

00:30:22.966 --> 00:30:25.102
So, what exactly are we looking for?

00:30:25.416 --> 00:30:27.033
I'll let you know when we find it.

00:31:21.856 --> 00:31:23.080
Sam!

00:31:33.406 --> 00:31:35.311
Hey, I'm here.
What is it?

00:31:35.637 --> 00:31:37.293
- What happened?
- Claire.

00:31:37.646 --> 00:31:39.282
- Where?
- She was here.

00:31:39.547 --> 00:31:40.571
Did she attack you?

00:31:40.918 --> 00:31:43.701
No. No, she was just like
reaching out to me.

00:31:44.135 --> 00:31:46.113
She was over there by the window.

00:31:58.298 --> 00:31:59.953
Here, help me move this.

00:32:00.866 --> 00:32:01.871
All right.

00:32:02.757 --> 00:32:03.882
I got it.

00:32:09.138 --> 00:32:10.893
Our little mystery word.

00:32:23.378 --> 00:32:25.233
Now the extra letters make sense.

00:32:30.858 --> 00:32:32.103
What is that?

00:32:33.546 --> 00:32:37.343
Spirits and certain remains
give off electromagnetic frequencies.

00:32:38.576 --> 00:32:40.773
So, if Claire's body was here,

00:32:41.226 --> 00:32:44.201
- that would indicate that?
- Yeah. Well, that's the theory.

00:33:09.637 --> 00:33:10.730
Yeah.

00:33:10.935 --> 00:33:13.232
Yeah, there's definitely something in there.

00:33:18.017 --> 00:33:19.283
You know,

00:33:20.117 --> 00:33:21.810
this is bothering me.

00:33:21.827 --> 00:33:23.952
Well, you are digging up a corpse.

00:33:23.956 --> 00:33:25.711
No, not that.

00:33:26.986 --> 00:33:29.183
That's, uh, pretty par for the course,
actually.

00:33:29.488 --> 00:33:30.823
Then what?

00:33:30.916 --> 00:33:31.740
It's just...

00:33:32.507 --> 00:33:36.001
I mean, no vengeful spirit
I've ever tussled with wanted to be wasted,

00:33:36.006 --> 00:33:39.031
so why the hell would Claire
lead us to her remains?

00:33:39.036 --> 00:33:40.773
Doesn't make any sense.

00:33:45.798 --> 00:33:46.872
All right. Here.

00:33:46.876 --> 00:33:47.862
Give me your hand.

00:34:22.818 --> 00:34:23.912
Her wrists.

00:34:24.628 --> 00:34:26.890
Yeah, they'd be bruised just like yours.

00:34:38.445 --> 00:34:40.000
That necklace mean something to you?

00:34:41.958 --> 00:34:43.153
I've seen it before.

00:34:45.068 --> 00:34:46.022
It's rare.

00:34:46.537 --> 00:34:48.712
It was custom-made over
on Carson street.

00:34:53.356 --> 00:34:54.783
I have one just like it.

00:34:56.576 --> 00:34:57.891
Pete gave it to me.

00:35:03.338 --> 00:35:04.993
Now this all makes perfect sense.

00:35:05.187 --> 00:35:06.173
I'm sorry?

00:35:06.175 --> 00:35:08.461
Yeah. You see,
Claire is not a vengeful spirit.

00:35:08.565 --> 00:35:09.821
She's a death omen.

00:35:10.597 --> 00:35:11.921
Excuse me?

00:35:12.177 --> 00:35:13.493
Claire's not killing anyone.

00:35:14.855 --> 00:35:16.080
She's trying to warn them.

00:35:18.406 --> 00:35:20.621
Sometimes spirits,
they don't want vengeance.

00:35:20.628 --> 00:35:23.332
They want justice, which is why
she led us here in the first place.

00:35:23.338 --> 00:35:25.463
She wants us to know who her killer is.

00:35:30.297 --> 00:35:32.840
Detective, how much do you know
about your partner?

00:35:36.188 --> 00:35:38.481
- Oh, my god.
- What?

00:35:40.057 --> 00:35:41.741
About a year ago,

00:35:41.926 --> 00:35:44.712
some heroin went missing from lockup.

00:35:45.038 --> 00:35:46.672
Obviously it was a cop.

00:35:47.366 --> 00:35:48.960
We never found out who did it.

00:35:50.398 --> 00:35:53.763
But whoever did it would need someone
to fence their product.

00:35:53.816 --> 00:35:55.210
Somebody like a heroin dealer.

00:35:57.246 --> 00:35:58.370
Somebody like Claire.

00:36:03.888 --> 00:36:06.431
So, I'm being extradited to St. Louis, huh?

00:36:09.417 --> 00:36:13.373
You just decided to transfer me yourself
800 miles at 2:00 in the morning?

00:36:18.456 --> 00:36:19.753
This can't be good.

00:36:20.566 --> 00:36:21.991
All right. Thanks.

00:36:22.737 --> 00:36:23.560
What is it?

00:36:23.745 --> 00:36:25.263
Pete just left the precinct.

00:36:25.495 --> 00:36:26.902
- With Dean.
- What?!

00:36:26.905 --> 00:36:30.311
He said the prisoner had to be transferred,
and he just took him.

00:36:30.315 --> 00:36:33.281
Dispatch has been calling,
but he won't answer the radio.

00:36:33.295 --> 00:36:34.361
Radio?

00:36:34.368 --> 00:36:36.440
- He took a county vehicle?
- Yeah.

00:36:36.445 --> 00:36:38.901
Then it should have a lojack.
You just got to get it turned on.

00:36:53.538 --> 00:36:54.520
Pee break?

00:36:54.587 --> 00:36:55.693
So soon?

00:36:56.358 --> 00:36:58.261
I think you might want
to get your prostate checked.

00:37:07.916 --> 00:37:09.302
Son of a bitch.

00:37:12.505 --> 00:37:14.882
Hey, I'm cool in the van.
You go do what you got to do.

00:37:20.077 --> 00:37:21.861
You're a cocky son of a bitch.

00:37:23.025 --> 00:37:26.252
You think those people in St. Louis
are gonna buy that crap you're paddling?

00:37:27.105 --> 00:37:28.460
Here's the thing.

00:37:28.987 --> 00:37:30.871
You're not gonna make it to St. Louis.

00:37:32.027 --> 00:37:33.252
You're gonna die

00:37:33.626 --> 00:37:34.960
trying to escape.

00:37:37.778 --> 00:37:39.112
Wait! Wait!

00:37:40.755 --> 00:37:41.991
Let's talk about this.

00:37:41.997 --> 00:37:43.830
You don't want to do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:37:45.596 --> 00:37:47.080
- Or maybe you do.
- Pete!

00:37:47.575 --> 00:37:48.701
Put the gun down.

00:37:48.967 --> 00:37:49.863
Diana?

00:37:50.705 --> 00:37:51.682
How'd you find me?

00:37:52.348 --> 00:37:53.611
I know about Claire.

00:37:53.615 --> 00:37:54.961
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:37:54.968 --> 00:37:56.793
Put the gun down!

00:37:56.797 --> 00:37:58.333
No, I don't think so.

00:37:59.046 --> 00:38:00.113
You're fast.

00:38:00.336 --> 00:38:02.071
Pretty sure I'm faster.

00:38:03.367 --> 00:38:04.381
Why are you doing this?

00:38:04.728 --> 00:38:06.252
I didn't do anything, Diana.

00:38:06.765 --> 00:38:08.191
It's a little late for that.

00:38:09.358 --> 00:38:10.700
It wasn't my fault.

00:38:11.595 --> 00:38:14.270
Claire was gonna turn me in.
I had no choice.

00:38:14.278 --> 00:38:15.342
And Tony?

00:38:15.715 --> 00:38:16.620
Karen?

00:38:16.726 --> 00:38:17.911
Same thing.

00:38:18.316 --> 00:38:20.722
Tony scrubbed the money.
Then he got skittish.

00:38:20.738 --> 00:38:22.540
And then he wanted to come clean.

00:38:22.545 --> 00:38:24.330
I'm sure he told Karen everything.

00:38:25.087 --> 00:38:27.223
It was a mess. I had to clean it up.

00:38:28.386 --> 00:38:29.441
I just panicked.

00:38:29.656 --> 00:38:32.031
How many more people
are gonna die over this, Pete?

00:38:32.038 --> 00:38:33.493
There's a way out.

00:38:35.035 --> 00:38:37.580
This Dean kid is a friggin' gift.

00:38:38.005 --> 00:38:39.983
We can pin the whole thing on him.

00:38:40.187 --> 00:38:44.270
Okay? No trial, nothing.
Just one more dead scumbag.

00:38:44.278 --> 00:38:45.231
Hey!

00:38:47.745 --> 00:38:49.021
No one will question it.

00:38:49.847 --> 00:38:51.683
Diana, please.

00:38:52.127 --> 00:38:53.511
I still love you.

00:38:59.915 --> 00:39:00.991
Thank you.

00:39:02.938 --> 00:39:04.072
Thank you.

00:39:13.395 --> 00:39:16.560
Then why don't you buy me another necklace,
you ass?

00:39:19.278 --> 00:39:21.390
Don't do it. Don't do it.

00:40:11.396 --> 00:40:12.481
You're doing all right?

00:40:13.678 --> 00:40:14.683
Not really.

00:40:15.947 --> 00:40:17.572
The death omen, Claire,

00:40:18.535 --> 00:40:19.931
what happens to her now?

00:40:20.125 --> 00:40:21.212
It should be over.

00:40:21.937 --> 00:40:23.301
She should be at rest.

00:40:25.036 --> 00:40:26.043
So, uh,

00:40:26.538 --> 00:40:27.890
what now, officer?

00:40:28.326 --> 00:40:29.933
Pete did confess to me.

00:40:30.038 --> 00:40:32.352
He screwed up both your cases royally.

00:40:32.428 --> 00:40:35.720
I'd say there's a good chance
that we can get your cases dismissed.

00:40:35.728 --> 00:40:38.360
- You could take care of that for us?
- I hope so.

00:40:38.557 --> 00:40:40.610
But the St. Louis murder charges?

00:40:40.898 --> 00:40:42.521
That's another story.

00:40:42.968 --> 00:40:44.633
I.. I can't help you.

00:40:46.226 --> 00:40:47.681
Unless

00:40:47.828 --> 00:40:50.681
I just happened to turn my back
and you walked away.

00:40:50.686 --> 00:40:52.823
I could tell them
that the suspects escaped.

00:40:52.956 --> 00:40:55.092
- Wait. Are you sure?
- Yeah, she's sure, Sam.

00:40:55.097 --> 00:40:57.953
You could lose your job over
something like that.

00:40:58.426 --> 00:41:01.061
Look, I just want you guys out there,
doing what you do best.

00:41:01.065 --> 00:41:01.962
Trust me.

00:41:02.205 --> 00:41:03.461
I'll sleep better at night.

00:41:04.595 --> 00:41:05.893
Listen, you need to watch your back.

00:41:05.908 --> 00:41:07.921
They're gonna be looking for both of you
right now.

00:41:08.877 --> 00:41:09.841
Get out of here.

00:41:10.345 --> 00:41:12.612
- I got to radio this in.
- Hey, uh...

00:41:13.096 --> 00:41:15.512
You wouldn't happen to know where
my car is by chance?

00:41:15.515 --> 00:41:18.311
It's at the impound yard on Robertson.

00:41:19.437 --> 00:41:20.522
Don't

00:41:20.688 --> 00:41:23.831
- even think about it.
- It's okay. It's all right. Don't worry.

00:41:24.106 --> 00:41:26.632
We'll just improvise.
We're pretty good at that.

00:41:26.635 --> 00:41:28.362
Yeah. I've noticed.

00:41:34.128 --> 00:41:36.001
- Nice lady.
- Yeah, for a cop.

00:41:37.045 --> 00:41:38.533
Did she look familiar to you?

00:41:38.538 --> 00:41:39.412
No. Why?

00:41:39.637 --> 00:41:41.611
I don't know. It's nothing.
Hey, you hungry?

00:41:41.617 --> 00:41:42.371
No.

00:41:42.378 --> 00:41:44.582
I have some reason
I could really go for some pea soup.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
